2 Options
*********

‘-c’
‘--csv’
     Output in CSV format (‘percentage%,count,value’) instead of the
     human-readable aligned columns.

‘-a’
‘--csvall’
     Like ‘--csv’, and also replace all whitespace within each value
     with commas.

‘-d N’
‘--decimal=N’
     Number of decimal places for percentages.  Default is ‘4’.

‘--numeric’
     Sort by the numeric value of the input lines rather than by
     occurrence count.  Useful when input lines are numbers and you want
     them in numeric order.

‘-m N’
‘--min=N’
     Exclude entries whose count is below N.  Excluded counts are
     accumulated into an ‘[excluded]’ summary line unless ‘--ignore’ is
     given.  By default, totals and percentages are recomputed from the
     remaining entries; see ‘--fullperc’ to override.

‘-x N’
‘--max=N’
     Exclude entries whose count is above N.  Operates identically to
     ‘--min’.

‘-f’
‘--fullperc’
     When used with ‘--min’ or ‘--max’, compute percentages from the
     full original total rather than the filtered count.

‘-i’
‘--ignore’
     When used with ‘--min’ or ‘--max’, suppress the ‘[excluded]’
     summary line.

‘-v’
‘--verbose’
     When used with ‘--min’ or ‘--max’, print to standard error the
     number of keys and total count before and after filtering.

‘-r’
‘--reverse’
     Reverse the sort order so the highest count (or highest numeric
     value with ‘--numeric’) appears first.

‘-h’
‘--help’
     Print a usage summary and exit.


