4 Examples
**********

Count file extensions under the current directory, least common first:

     find . -type f | sed 's/.*\.//' | psort

   Show the five most common HTTP status codes (highest count first):

     awk '{print $9}' access.log | psort -r | head -5

   Word frequencies, keeping only words appearing at least 10 times,
percentages computed from the full document total:

     tr -cs 'A-Za-z' '\n' < doc.txt | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | psort --min 10 --fullperc

   Numeric distribution of response times, sorted by value:

     awk '{print $NF}' timings.log | psort --numeric

   CSV of entries with counts between 5 and 100, full-total percentages:

     cat data.txt | psort -c --min 5 --max 100 --fullperc


