6.1 Methodology
===============

Each port was run *100 times* against a large input file containing
2,289,195 lines of file path data.  Program output was discarded; only
timing metrics were captured using:

     /usr/bin/time -f "real=%e user=%U sys=%S mem=%M" \
         psort_c < /tmp/find.data > /dev/null

   Metrics collected per run:

REAL
     Wall-clock elapsed time, in seconds.
USER
     User-space CPU time, in seconds.
SYS
     Kernel (system-call) CPU time, in seconds.
MEM
     Peak resident set size (‘%M’ from ‘time’), in kilobytes.

   Statistics reported: minimum, maximum, mean, and population standard
deviation (n = 100 runs per variant).


